---
// One patient's record, in the workspace (the Patients tab lit): a head
// of the facts that decide the next step — name, age, mobile, the HMO card,
// what they owe (finance roles), the safety line, the note for the dentist
// and the desk's note — then four tabs
// switched in place, in a row that stays at the top of the screen
// (./_record/RecordNav.astro, ./_record/sections.ts): Today (./_record/Today.astro:
// this visit's checklist, what is coming and the next check-up, what needs
// attention, the last visit) · Patient info (details, health, blood
// pressure, consent) · Chart & plan (the chart, the plan and work done, lab
// cases, X-rays and photos, HMO approvals, payment plans) · Treatment record
// (the ledger, notes, prescriptions and letters, statements, texts). The tab is
// in the address (#chart, #treatment-record, or any card's anchor: #health,
// #rx, …, each read through TAB_OF), so a reload, a post that comes back and a
// link all land on it. Money is shown only to people who may bill here
// (canBill in src/lib/invoices.ts), like the Finances tab.
//
// Drawn in the soft, very simple template (docs/workspace-redesign.md, "The
// soft template" and "Very simple"): the patient's avatar and a few facts in
// one line with the chart no. as a small reference pill — for people who may
// bill, "Owes ₱…" (or "In credit ₱…") as a link to their statements in
// Finances; Edit details and New booking (the Dashboard's booking panel, the
// patient filled in), both quiet, since a screen's one teal button is its
// tab's; then the safety line, in plain words and never buttons
// (./_record/SafetyLine.astro: the allergies, or which kind of none, the
// conditions, the medicines, a blood pressure, a clearance, under 18), which
// the tab row pins while the record is scrolled; the note for the dentist in
// full; the desk's note (deskNoteOf: patient.notes less the import's own
// lines) in one quiet line. Everything written into the record (a note, a treatment,
// a reading, a prescription, a file, a plan item, a lab case, an LOA, a
// payment plan, a letter, a charge) is under Add ▾ at the end of the tab row.
// The pages' own pieces are in ./_ui/ (patients.css, HealthLists, Callout,
// Head, Glyph).
//
// Every side panel lives outside the tabs, so it opens over whichever tab is
// in view, and its form posts back=<that tab>: a save comes back to the tab
// with its saved line at the top (./_record/SavedLine.astro), and a refused
// post comes back over it with the panel open again. A card's own button (the
// next check-up, a plan row, a lab case …) posts no back: it comes back to its
// card, with the saved line (or the refusal) inside the card, under its title.
//
// Every query runs inside withClinic(), so row-level security decides whether
// this patient exists here; a patient of another clinic (or a made-up id) is
// a 404 on reading and on every post. Opening the record writes
// patient.view to the audit log.
//
// The odontogram is src/components/Odontogram.astro. It gains the palette's
// record actions and the plan/done marks (props `actions`, `work`); its
// offline logic (the kept copy of this page, changes waiting on the device)
// is untouched. A copy served offline opens on Chart & plan, and a notice the
// chart raises (a colleague's newer finding, changes waiting) brings it
// forward; Add ▾ hides there and whenever the device is offline. The palette's
// Add to plan, Treatment done and Clinical note open Add to plan, Record a
// treatment and the note (_record/TreatmentPanels, _record/NotePanel, outside
// the tabs) over the chart on that tooth; they post back=chart, the save lands
// on the chart with its line (?back=chart), and closing one gives focus back
// to the tooth.
//
// Four forms post back to this page, each with the CSRF token, checked before
// anything else (a miss comes back with ?stale=1):
//   intent=health   allergies, conditions, medicines, a note.
//                   saveHealth() in src/lib/health.ts: a new medical_history
//                   version under the person who saved it, audit
//                   health.update. A save that started from an older version
//                   than the newest writes nothing and shows what the other
//                   person saved.
//   intent=consent  the privacy notice agreed at the desk (DeskConsent.astro),
//                   recordDeskConsent(): channel 'desk', who agreed (the
//                   patient, or a parent or guardian, named), audit
//                   consent.desk. Under 18 by the birth date on file, only a
//                   parent or guardian; with none on file, the desk says which.
//   intent=paper    a consent signed on paper (recordPaperConsent): a printed
//                   copy of the notice in force, dated on a day it was in
//                   force, or the clinic's own form (026). Audit consent.paper
//                   / consent.paper_form.
//   intent=details  Edit details (a side panel): name, chart no., birth date,
//                   sex, mobile, email, address, HMO, emergency contact, notes —
//                   updateDetails() in src/lib/import.ts, audit patient.update;
//                   a changed birth date is kept in the health history as the
//                   health form kept it (saveBirth() in src/lib/health.ts: a
//                   version with the change from and to, audit
//                   patient.birth_date), in the same transaction, and one
//                   someone else changed since the panel opened takes back the
//                   whole save and says what is on file now. Saved, it lands on
//                   Today (?saved=details, or ?saved=birth when the birth date
//                   changed); refused, over the tab it was opened on. Opened from the Dashboard's desk note
//                   (?open=details&dash=<visit>), the form carries the visit in
//                   a hidden dash, and a save goes back to the Dashboard with that
//                   visit open (only a visit of this patient's).
// All need staff_access.can_edit_records for this branch (every role has it
// today; see canEditRecords()). On success the page redirects to itself
// (?saved=…) so a reload does not post again; on a problem it renders again
// with what was typed.
//
// Patient forms (the QR code on the desk, src/lib/patient-forms.ts): a form
// added to this record comes here with ?saved=form&form=<id>, and the page
// says what it wrote (the consents as the record now has them: from the form,
// already on file, or none because the record makes the patient a minor who
// signed for themself; the allergies, conditions and medicines kept from the
// record), and lists each detail the form says differently, or a mobile or
// email the desk did not tick, with "Use <it>" (a fifth post, intent
// form-use: useFormDetail writes that one detail and comes back with
// &used=<field>). Names and the birth date are never offered. The page
// says what went on the record and, for a patient already on file, what the
// form says differently (kept as on file; Edit details changes it). The
// Overview shows what the latest form says about this visit (the reason, what
// is bothering them); Consent lists every form added here — when it was sent,
// who signed, the consents it wrote — with its answers and a printout
// (../forms/<id>/). A health version from a form reads "from the patient
// forms (QR-7K2F)".
export const prerender = false;

import ClinicLayout from '../../../../layouts/Clinic.astro';
import Csrf from '../../../../components/Csrf.astro';
import DeskConsent from '../../../../components/DeskConsent.astro';
import ConsentForms from './_record/ConsentForms.astro';
import Odontogram from '../../../../components/Odontogram.astro';
import Pane from '../../../../components/ws/Pane.astro';
import Chip from '../../../../components/ws/Chip.astro';
import Empty from '../../../../components/ws/Empty.astro';
import SidePanel from '../../../../components/ws/SidePanel.astro';
import Icon from '../../../../components/ws/Icon.astro';
import Avatar from '../../../../components/ws/Avatar.astro';
import Head from './_ui/Head.astro';
import Callout from './_ui/Callout.astro';
import HealthLists from './_ui/HealthLists.astro';
import Glyph from './_ui/Glyph.astro';
import './_ui/patients.css';
import './_forms/forms.css';
import './_record/record.css';
import TreatmentRecord from './_record/TreatmentRecord.astro';
import VisitPanels from './_record/VisitPanels.astro';
import TreatmentPanels from './_record/TreatmentPanels.astro';
import ChartOffer from './_record/ChartOffer.astro';
import NotePanel from './_record/NotePanel.astro';
import Signature from './_record/Signature.astro';
import Treatment from './_record/Treatment.astro';
import Notes from './_record/Notes.astro';
import Prescriptions from './_record/Prescriptions.astro';
import Files from './_record/Files.astro';
import RecallCard from './_record/RecallCard.astro';
import Vitals from './_record/Vitals.astro';
import Letters from './_record/Letters.astro';
import Loas from './_record/Loas.astro';
import PayPlans from './_record/PayPlans.astro';
import RecordNav from './_record/RecordNav.astro';
import SavedLine from './_record/SavedLine.astro';
import SafetyLine from './_record/SafetyLine.astro';
import { safetyItems, safetyLine } from './_record/safety';
import Who from './_record/Who.astro';
import VisitStrip from './_record/VisitStrip.astro';
import Today from './_record/Today.astro';
import { thisVisitPlan, needsAttention, dayOf } from './_record/today';
import { remindersFor, reminderWords } from '../../../../lib/reminder-state';
import { whenText, shortName as drShort } from '../../../../lib/schedule';
import { ANCHOR, CARD_HUE, OPEN_PANEL, TABS, backOf, landingSection, savedCard, tabOf } from './_record/sections';
import { shellLinks } from '../../../../components/ws/routes';
import { requireWorkspace } from '../../../../lib/workspace';
import { withClinic } from '../../../../lib/db';
import { csrfOk, csrfToken, CSRF_MESSAGE } from '../../../../lib/csrf';
import { hit, waitText, LIMITS } from '../../../../lib/throttle';
import {
  LISTS, NOTE_MAX, NAME_MAX, manilaToday, ageOn, ageText, when, day, oneLine, readHealthForm, saveHealth, readHealth,
  canEditRecords, readConsents, noticeInForce, recordDeskConsent, versionChanges, listText, answered, dateText, capitalise,
  consentInForce, readPaperForms, readPaperForm, recordPaperConsent, PAPER_WORDS, recheckHealth, readBirth, saveBirth,
  type HealthAnswers, type HealthVersion, type AgreedAs, type PaperIn,
} from '../../../../lib/health';
import { readPersonForm, updateDetails, hmoSuggestions, deskNoteOf, importNotesOf, SEXES, NOTES_MAX, type PersonIn } from '../../../../lib/import';
import { pesos, statementNo, STATUS as BILL_STATUS, fromDb } from '../../../../lib/invoices';
import { prettyPhone } from '../../../../lib/messages';
import { hmos } from '../../../../data/directory';
import { CONDITION_LABEL, surfaceSummary, type ToothCondition, type ToothMark, type Surface, type Notation } from '../../../../data/demo';
import { patientForms, getForm, compareWithRecord, useFormDetail, healthLists, answerText, FIELDS, TAKEABLE, type FormConsentState } from '../../../../lib/patient-forms';
import { signedText } from './_forms/words';
import { can } from '../../../../lib/can';
import { mayManage } from '../../../../lib/roles';
import type { PtrFix } from '../../../../lib/ptr';
import { loadClinical, loadChartChanges, recordAction, RECORD_INTENTS, RX_ROWS, SECTION_OF as RECORD_SECTION, type Outcome, type RecordProblem, type RxItem } from '../../../../lib/record';
import { loadExtra, extraAction, bpWords, EXTRA_INTENTS, EXTRA_ANCHOR, SECTION_OF as EXTRA_SECTION } from '../../../../lib/record-extra';
import { loadVisitConsents } from '../../../../lib/visit-consent';
import { Refused } from '../../../../lib/refused';
import { loadConsentDocuments, mayAttest, capacityNote } from '../../../../lib/consent-docs';
import { intakeGates } from '../../../../lib/intake';
import { loadVisits, VISIT_STATUS, type StripVisit } from '../../../../lib/visit-record';
import { buildLedger, loadLedgerMoney, loadRecallsSet } from '../../../../lib/treatment-record';
import { offerFor } from '../../../../lib/chart-write';
import { calloutWorthy } from '../../../../lib/chart-offer';
import { chartSession } from '../../../api/chart';

const ws = await requireWorkspace(Astro);
if (ws instanceof Response) return ws;
const { clinic, session, branches } = ws;
const money = can(clinic, 'finance.bill');
const links = shellLinks(clinic.slug);

const UUID = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;
const patientId = Astro.params.patient ?? '';
const notFound = () => new Response('No such patient', { status: 404 });
if (!UUID.test(patientId)) return notFound();
const here = `/c/${clinic.slug}/patients/${patientId}/`;
const HMO_NAMES = new Map(hmos.map((h) => [h.id, h.name]));
const q = Astro.url.searchParams;
// The tag of this sign-in (the chart's own): a chart write from the record is made only from a page drawn under it (p01 step 2).
const chartSid = chartSession(session);

// What a post left behind for the page to show.
let healthProblems: string[] = [];
let posted: { answers: HealthAnswers; base: string } | null = null;
let conflict: { latest: HealthVersion | null } | null = null;
let consentProblem: string | null = null;
let givenBy = '';
let agreedAs: AgreedAs | null = null;
let paperState: { open: boolean; problem: string | null; values: Partial<PaperIn> } = { open: false, problem: null, values: {} };
let detailsProblems: string[] = [];
let detailsPosted: PersonIn | null = null;
// The birth date Edit details was posted with, and the one it was drawn with (on a conflict, the one on file now).
let birthPosted: { value: string; was: string } | null = null;
// Edit details opened from the Dashboard (?open=details&dash=<visit>): the visit to go back to once it is saved.
let detailsDash: string | null = null;
let formUseProblem: string | null = null;
// A clinical-record post (Treatment, Notes, Prescriptions, Files, the next check-up) that was refused.
let recordProblem: RecordProblem | null = null;
let rxTyped: RxItem[] = [];
// "No change" on the This visit strip (intent health-checked) that was refused: its sentence, on the strip.
let stripProblem: string | null = null;
// The section (or tab) a post came back to.
let backTo: string | null = null;
/** A refused clinical-record post (src/lib/refused.ts): thrown out of the transaction so nothing half-done is kept, its outcome as the detail. */
type RecordRefusal = Extract<Outcome, { ok: false }>;
/** The intents whose refusal is said in their card, not in a panel (a plan item's Mark done from its row too, which
 *  posts no back): it comes back to that card's section whatever `back` a post carried. */
const INLINE_REFUSAL = new Set(['plan-remove', 'lab-next', 'file-remove', 'loa-cancel', 'payplan-stop', 'recall-done', 'recall-clear', 'chart-apply']);

if (Astro.request.method === 'POST') {
  const form = await Astro.request.formData();
  if (!csrfOk(Astro.cookies, form)) return Astro.redirect(here + '?stale=1', 303);
  const intent = String(form.get('intent') ?? '');
  // Same allowance as the chart: a person saving never meets it; a script does.
  const rate = await hit('record:s:' + session.staffId, ...LIMITS.chart.staff);
  const slow = rate.allowed ? null : 'Too many saves at once. ' + waitText(rate.retryAfter);
  // The visit a chairside post was for (036): the This visit strip's forms and the panels it opens carry it,
  // and the page comes back with ?visit=<id> kept, so the strip is still there after the save.
  const postedVisit = UUID.test(String(form.get('visit') ?? '')) ? String(form.get('visit')) : null;
  const to = (qs: string, hash: string) => `${here}?${[postedVisit ? `visit=${postedVisit}` : '', qs].filter(Boolean).join('&')}${hash ? `#${hash}` : ''}`;

  if (intent === 'health') {
    // The answers only: the birth date is in Edit details now (the form sends none, so saveHealth leaves it as it is).
    // A form drawn before the birth date moved still carries it (birth_was): kept, as saveHealth always kept it.
    backTo = 'health';
    const { answers, birth, problems } = readHealthForm(form);
    const legacy = form.has('birth_was') ? { birth, birthWas: oneLine(form.get('birth_was')) || null } : { birth: null, birthWas: null };
    let base = String(form.get('base') ?? '');
    if (slow) problems.unshift(slow);
    if (problems.length === 0) {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? saveHealth(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, base, answers, ...legacy })
          : ({ kind: 'denied' } as const));
      if (r.kind === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r.kind === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(to(r.answers ? 'saved=health' : 'saved=birth', r.answers ? 'health' : 'overview'), 303);
      if (r.kind === 'unchanged') return Astro.redirect(to('saved=nothing', 'health'), 303);
      if (r.kind === 'denied') problems.push('Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.');
      if (r.kind === 'conflict') {
        conflict = { latest: r.latest };
        // The next Save starts from what is on file now.
        base = r.latest?.id ?? 'none';
      }
    }
    healthProblems = problems;
    posted = { answers, base };
  } else if (intent === 'consent') {
    backTo = 'consent';
    givenBy = oneLine(form.get('given_by_name'));
    const who = String(form.get('agreed_as') ?? '');
    agreedAs = who === 'patient' || who === 'guardian' ? who : null;
    if (slow) consentProblem = slow;
    else if (form.get('agreed') !== '1') consentProblem = 'Tick the box that says they agreed, once they have. Nothing was recorded.';
    else if (givenBy.length > NAME_MAX) consentProblem = `Keep the name under ${NAME_MAX} characters.`;
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? recordDeskConsent(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, version: String(form.get('version') ?? ''), givenBy: givenBy || null, agreedAs })
          : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=consent#consent`, 303);
      if (r === 'already') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=consent-already#consent`, 303);
      consentProblem = {
        denied: 'Your account cannot record consent at this branch. Ask the owner.',
        who: 'Choose who is agreeing: the patient, 18 or over, or a parent or guardian. Nothing was recorded.',
        minor: 'The birth date on file makes the patient under 18, so a parent or guardian agrees for them. Ask them to type their name. Nothing was recorded.',
        'guardian-name': 'A parent or guardian is agreeing, so they type their name. Nothing was recorded.',
        'no-notice': 'No privacy notice is in force, so there is nothing to record.',
        changed: 'The privacy notice changed while this page was open. Show the patient the new one below.',
      }[r];
      if (r === 'minor') agreedAs = 'guardian';
    }
  } else if (intent === 'paper') {
    backTo = 'consent';
    const { paper, problems } = readPaperForm(form);
    paperState = { open: true, problem: slow ?? (problems.length ? problems.join(' ') : null), values: paper };
    if (!paperState.problem) {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? recordPaperConsent(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, ...paper })
          : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=paper#consent-paper`, 303);
      paperState.problem = r === 'denied' ? 'Your account cannot record consent at this branch. Ask the owner.' : `${PAPER_WORDS[r]} Nothing was recorded.`;
    }
  } else if (intent === 'details') {
    // Refused, it comes back over the tab it was opened on (its back); saved, it lands on Today.
    backTo = backOf(form.get('back')) ?? 'overview';
    const { person, problems } = readPersonForm(form);
    detailsPosted = person;
    // The birth date (its history is kept in the health history: saveBirth), and the one the panel was drawn with.
    const birthIn = readBirth(form.get('birth_date'));
    if (birthIn.problem) problems.push(birthIn.problem);
    birthPosted = { value: oneLine(form.get('birth_date')), was: oneLine(form.get('birth_was')) };
    const dashIn = String(form.get('dash') ?? '');
    detailsDash = UUID.test(dashIn) ? dashIn.toLowerCase() : null;
    if (slow) problems.unshift(slow);
    if (!problems.length) {
      // One transaction: a birth date someone else changed since the panel opened takes back the rest of the save too.
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => {
        if (!(await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))) return 'denied' as const;
        const u = await updateDetails(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, p: person });
        if (u !== 'saved') return u;
        const b = await saveBirth(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, birth: birthIn.birth, birthWas: birthPosted!.was || null });
        if (b.kind === 'none') return 'none' as const;
        if (b.kind === 'conflict') throw new Refused<{ onFile: string | null }>('birth', { onFile: b.birth });
        return b.kind === 'saved' ? ('birth' as const) : ('saved' as const);
      }).catch((e) => { if (e instanceof Refused) return { moved: (e as Refused<{ onFile: string | null }>).detail.onFile }; throw e; });
      if (r === 'none') return notFound();
      if ((r === 'saved' || r === 'birth') && detailsDash) {
        // Back to the Dashboard with that visit's panel open, showing the new note: only a visit of this patient's.
        const v = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => (await tx.query(
          `select to_char(starts_at at time zone 'Asia/Manila', 'YYYY-MM-DD') as ymd from appointment where id = $1 and patient_id = $2`, [detailsDash, patientId])).rows[0]);
        if (v) return Astro.redirect(`/c/${clinic.slug}/?${v.ymd === manilaToday() ? '' : `date=${v.ymd}&`}booking=${detailsDash}`, 303);
      }
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=details`, 303);
      if (r === 'birth') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=birth`, 303);
      if (r === 'denied') problems.push('Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.');
      else if ('moved' in r) {
        // The next Save starts from the birth date on file now; what this person typed stays in the field.
        problems.push(`Someone changed the birth date on file to ${dateText(r.moved) ?? 'none'} after this panel opened. Check it with the patient, then save again.`);
        birthPosted.was = r.moved ?? '';
      } else problems.push(r.taken);
    }
    detailsProblems = problems;
  } else if (RECORD_INTENTS.has(intent) || EXTRA_INTENTS.has(intent)) {
    // The clinical record (src/lib/record.ts): every intent checks canEditRecords in its own transaction.
    // A panel's form posts back=<the tab it was opened over> (the chart's palette: back=chart): saved or refused, it
    // comes back to that tab. A card's own buttons post no back and come back to their card.
    const postedBack = backOf(form.get('back'));
    // Refused by the rate limit before anything was read: the intent's own section, as its refusal would have said.
    const outcome = slow
      ? ({ ok: false, section: RECORD_SECTION[intent] ?? EXTRA_SECTION[intent] ?? 'overview', problem: slow, values: {} } as Extract<Outcome, { ok: false }>)
      : await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => {
          const o = EXTRA_INTENTS.has(intent)
            ? await extraAction(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, canBill: money, hmoNames: HMO_NAMES }, intent, form)
            : await recordAction(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, sid: chartSid }, intent, form);
          if (o !== 'none' && !o.ok) throw new Refused<RecordRefusal>(o.problem, o);
          return o;
        }).catch((e) => { if (e instanceof Refused) return (e as Refused<RecordRefusal>).detail; throw e; });
    if (outcome === 'none') return notFound();
    if (outcome.ok) {
      // A treatment the chart could show lands on its offer (treated=…, #chart-offer), which is drawn on Chart & plan;
      // a panel's save on the tab it was opened over (back=…, #<tab>, its saved line at the top); anything else on its
      // card (savedCard in ./_record/sections.ts, where the page then draws its saved line), else its anchor (ANCHOR,
      // EXTRA_ANCHOR), else its section.
      const qs = [`saved=${encodeURIComponent(outcome.saved)}`, ...Object.entries(outcome.qs ?? {}).map(([k, v]) => `${k}=${encodeURIComponent(v)}`), postedBack ? `back=${postedBack}` : ''].filter(Boolean).join('&');
      const hash = outcome.qs?.treated ? 'chart-offer' : postedBack ?? savedCard(outcome.saved) ?? ANCHOR[intent] ?? EXTRA_ANCHOR[intent] ?? outcome.section;
      return Astro.redirect(to(qs, hash), 303);
    }
    // Refused (the rate limit too): a panel's post comes back over the tab it was opened on, with the panel open
    // again; a card's own button (its sentence is drawn in the card) comes back to the card's section.
    backTo = (INLINE_REFUSAL.has(intent) || (intent === 'plan-status' && !postedBack) ? null : postedBack) ?? outcome.section;
    recordProblem = { intent, text: outcome.problem, values: outcome.values };
    if (intent === 'rx-add') {
      const col = (k: string) => form.getAll(k).map((x) => String(x));
      const [dr, st, qt, sg] = [col('drug'), col('strength'), col('qty'), col('sig')];
      rxTyped = Array.from({ length: RX_ROWS }, (_, i) => ({ drug: dr[i] ?? '', strength: st[i] ?? '', qty: qt[i] ?? '', sig: sg[i] ?? '' }));
    }
  } else if (intent === 'health-checked') {
    // "No change" on the This visit strip: the health history asked again today and still true (recheckHealth).
    if (slow) stripProblem = slow;
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id)) ? recheckHealth(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId }) : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(to('saved=checked', ''), 303);
      if (r === 'today') return Astro.redirect(to('saved=checked-today', ''), 303);
      stripProblem = r === 'denied' ? 'Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.'
        : 'There is no health history on file to check yet. Ask the patient and save the answers in Health.';
    }
  } else if (intent === 'form-use') {
    // One detail from an added patient form onto the record ("Use 0917 555 0199").
    backTo = 'overview';
    const formId = String(form.get('form') ?? '');
    const field = String(form.get('field') ?? '');
    if (slow) formUseProblem = slow;
    else if (!UUID.test(formId) || !TAKEABLE.has(field)) formUseProblem = 'That detail cannot be taken from the form. Nothing was changed.';
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, (tx) => useFormDetail(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, formId, field }));
      if (r === 'saved' || r === 'same') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?form=${formId}&used=${encodeURIComponent(field)}#overview`, 303);
      formUseProblem = r === 'not-allowed' ? 'Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.' : 'That form is not on this record any more. Nothing was changed.';
    }
  }
}

const data = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => {
